NOTES={
'segment.py:LabelComponents':'The current routine scans horizontal runs, merges touching previous-row labels through a path-compressed Find helper, and compacts roots at the end. Half-open run endpoints plus the overlap tests include diagonal contact. Renaming Find does not alter the labelling idea; compare partitions rather than integer label IDs.',
'segment.py:Skeletonize':'The Ring helper constructs eight shifted neighbours from a zero-padded current mask. Every sub-pass calculates deletion eligibility before applying all deletions together. The second sub-pass uses the complementary triplet tests. This is still Zhang--Suen; it is not an exact Euclidean medial axis or measured stroke order.',
'segment.py:_LetterHeight':'Connected-piece sizes provide a typical letter scale when row-peak spacing might describe ascenders and descenders of one line instead of separate lines. It is a fallback measurement, not a recognised character label.',
'segment.py:LinePitch':'The current pitch floor is PEAK_MIN_PITCH_XH times estimated letter height. Candidate peaks exceed six percent of the smoothed maximum. Median adjacent spacing is accepted only if above the floor; otherwise autocorrelation, a 2.2-times-letter-height fallback and finally 48 pixels are tried. The retired TRUST_ALL_PEAK_GAPS bypass is absent.',
'segment.py:Deskew':'The page is reduced by a two-to-one box average; a further reduction supplies the trial mask. Seventeen trial angles from minus four to plus four degrees are scored, then both full and working grey images are rotated and the mask rebuilt. This function neither accepts nor records a timer.',
'segment.py:DropArtifactPieces':'The current artefact policy uses a pitch-scaled closed mask, component measurements, paper location and brightness-ratio evidence before discarding whole pieces. Its geometry guards are project rules. A discarded component is not automatically proven non-writing; inspect sparse punctuation and page-edge handwriting.',
'segment.py:LineCentres':'Strongest-first peak suppression enforces a separation of 0.6 pitch. The optional mergeValley parameter controls repeated merging of neighbours with shallow intervening valleys. At the module default 1.0 the merging loop does not run. It is distinct from seam optimisation.',
'segment.py:_SheetCrop':'This helper supplies a central paper-oriented crop for the orientation score. It changes evidence supplied to axis estimation, not the final physical page boundary by itself.',
'segment.py:LineAxisScore':'The implemented score is the fraction of row sums below 0.35 times their mean after downsampling and sheet cropping. It is not the coefficient-of-variation score described in some older comments. Empty/very small masks produce zero.',
'segment.py:UprightPage':'Scores the original and a ninety-degree rotation and accepts the turn only if the rotated score exceeds 1.35 times the guarded original score. It resolves the writing axis, not a one-hundred-eighty-degree inversion.',
'segment.py:DropSolidCrops':'Measures the fraction of crop pixels below grey level 128. A crop is dropped only if above 15 percent and three times the crop-population median. If all would be dropped, the original list is returned. These are crop fractions, not per-row ratios or the 15-percent ownership rule.',
'segment.py:SegmentLines':'Current signature is SegmentLines(page, mergeValley=None). It calls deskew, structure removal, artefact filtering, centres, seams, ownership, full-resolution crop construction and solid-crop rejection. It returns lines, debug arrays and summary information. No timer keyword exists: the server currently times this complete call as one stage.',
'recognise.py:PaperCRNNNumpy':'The callable method is Forward with a capital F. Two, four and six convolution blocks are separated by two spatial pools; a height maximum yields 160 feature columns for a 64 by 640 input. Two bidirectional recurrent layers feed the text head. The constructor default reader is the scratch checkpoint; START.sh selects the joint reader through READER_WEIGHTS instead.',
'recognise.py:ReadTextScored':'Calls model.Forward and returns the greedy transcript plus mean best-class log probability over every frame. Blank-dominated frames contribute. This score is used to choose page inversion; it is not transcript probability, edit accuracy or a calibrated confidence that the text is correct.',
'recognise.py:ReadText':'Delegates to ReadTextScored and keeps only the string. The result depends on the already-loaded model and complete crop preparation; changing a checkpoint filename does not replace an existing model object.',
'recognise.py:AuthorClassifierCNNNumpy':'The current method is Forward. After the convolution backbone, height maximum and width average, a 96-unit hidden affine/ReLU head produces one logit per saved writer mapping entry. Dropout is skipped at inference. The default file is author_shape_11w_pw170_scratch_weights.npz; the server INK_MODEL and SHAPE_MODEL variables reference this same loaded object.',
'recognise.py:ClassifyImage':'Optionally binarises, thins and redilates the input, fits the fixed canvas, calls model.Forward and returns argmax index plus the full softmax vector. The optional authorMapping argument is not used to remap outputs. Decode indices with model.authorMapping; its order is part of the checkpoint contract.',
'style.py:TracePolylines':'The current implementation is the split-at-junction tracer directly; the older alternate through-junction tracer and feature switch are absent. It builds a pixel graph, suppresses redundant diagonal edges when an orthogonal connection exists, visits edges, prunes short chains and rejoins compatible endpoint directions. It estimates a useful drawing order, not the historical pen chronology.',
'style.py:_TrimLigatureTails':'Removes eligible low outward tails left at character cuts and records connection endpoints. Guards retain a minimum body and reject suspicious climbing tails. These local rules can confuse genuine flourishes with connectors; the thresholds are project heuristics.',
'style.py:ExtractLineGlyphs':'Uses model.Forward, forced CTC alignment, an estimated body band and slant, then one shared strictly increasing cut array. It thins the full line before cell splitting, traces paths, handles dots/crossbars and stores upright x-height coordinates plus lead/advance metadata. A legal transcript alignment is not a verified character boundary.',
'style.py:BuildLetterPrior':'Pools descriptors across writers by character, requires a minimum sample count, takes a componentwise median and unit-normalises it. It supplies a rejection reference, not another writer glyph to be copied. Absent priors must not be interpreted as evidence of a perfect glyph.',
'style.py:BuildAuthorProfile':'Rejects low-confidence source lines when enough are available, accumulates measured style, filters each character pool, computes prior and consensus, and stores variants, denoised prototypes and medoids. The profile stores ink-related reference statistics even though current RenderTrajectory uses uniform ink. Such stored metadata is not evidence that a live branch consumes it.',
'synthesise.py:_GapRange':'Caches a gap interval in profile _gapRange from the ninetieth percentile of stored advance minus lead minus width. Bounds MIN_LETTER_GAP_XH and MAX_LETTER_GAP_XH constrain it. Later parameter or pool edits may need this cached interval recalculated.',
'synthesise.py:_Advance':'Uses the selected glyph own lead and width plus a bounded residual gap. Editing only the profile letterAdvance summary does not generally change normal stored glyph placement.',
'synthesise.py:_CoreGlyph':'The current source always prefers profile idealMedoid if acceptable; the older IDEAL_SOURCE switch is absent. It falls back to the designed alphabet when the stored representative is absent or too rough. The profile connectedness threshold 0.5 chooses print versus cursive fallback style.',
'synthesise.py:_GlyphSource':'Sorts a character pool by prior distance and offers only the first _ELIGIBLE_VARIANTS, currently five. Rank weight is 1/(1+1.4*i), with an entry-height compatibility factor when joining. A probability policy may substitute the representative; case-related, similar, designed and blank fallbacks cover missing characters. It records own/core/case/similar/fallback provenance rather than silently treating all shapes as captured.',
'synthesise.py:StyleCalibration':'Always used unless a caller passes an explicit _cal into SynthesizeText. The retired USE_STYLE_CALIBRATION switch is absent. A cache keyed by authorId, physical x-height and render density stores corrections from a short fixed probe. Changes to other profile fields can reuse an old correction unless the cache is invalidated.',
'synthesise.py:_Ligature':'The current connector uses the shallow project construction; the optional tangent-ligature implementation and switch are absent. A join adds new ink that was not observed in either stored character. It should not be represented as recovered original pen motion.',
'synthesise.py:_BodyStroke':'Selects the body path and eligible entry/exit rather than joining via dots or crossbars. Flatness and small-horizontal-span guards address ambiguous skeleton ordering. The former JOIN_ANATOMY feature switch is absent; the actual helper determines the rule.',
'synthesise.py:SynthesizeText':'Always computes or accepts style correction, clamps writer slant, suppresses joins below connectedness 0.45, and otherwise uses connEff equal to measured connectedness. There is no JOIN_PROB_CAP or JOIN_LEGIBILITY_COUPLING in this tree. Glyph variants, bounded spacing, jitter, integrated drift, collision clearance and compatible joins create millimetre paths; lineStepMm is (ascender - descender + 0.85) times x-height.',
'synthesise.py:RenderTrajectory':'Current accepted parameters are traj, pxPerMm, padMm, strokePx and size. There are no profile or uniformInk parameters. Rendering always uses the uniform-width path, default width fraction 0.085 and blur fraction 0.30. Optional size performs a subsequent raster resize and can change aspect ratio if both dimensions are specified independently.',
'synthesise.py:_LineLogProbs':'Fits the rendered crop to the reader canvas and calls reader.Forward. It is a model-scoring input path, not a geometric measurement of the physical gantry output.',
'synthesise.py:SynthesizeJointBestOf':'The direct function default is six tries, while server DEFAULT_TRIES is fourteen unless WEBAPP_TRIES overrides it. Each candidate is rendered and scored by text edit agreement and requested-writer probability using their harmonic mean. Up to three repair rounds target two new weak positions per round; only an improved complete score commits the repair. Search stopping thresholds and seed spacing 977 are heuristics, not published optima.',
'reproduce.py:GantryConfig':'Current fields include gearing, bounds, origin, margins, ruling fractions, feeds, decimation, pen dwell and endpoint/ring join distances. They do not include ignoreRuling, fitToRuling or accelMmS2. Properties derive commanded steps/mm from 200 full steps, sixteen microsteps and forty millimetres per revolution; controller calibration later uses measured per-axis factors.',
'reproduce.py:XhForRuling':'Chooses x-height before line wrapping from profile xhOverPitch if between 0.15 and 0.90, otherwise rulingXhFrac, multiplied by lineHeightMm. An optional plain synthesis probe reduces size if the tallest line exceeds rulingMaxExtent. It supplies a size constraint, not guaranteed actual line spacing.',
'reproduce.py:_TallestLine':'Groups trajectory strokes around the stored synthesis pitch and measures each row extent for the size cap. Grouping can be imperfect when stroke geometry spans neighbouring rows; the returned extent is a geometric proxy.',
'reproduce.py:ToMachine':'Uniformly shrinks only when work-area width/height requires it, then uses each detected line centre to remove baseline wander while retaining synthesis pitch times scale. There is no selectable ignoreRuling branch. Coordinates remain y-up; top alignment and margin/offset subtraction do not introduce a second image-axis flip.',
'reproduce.py:SetPenLines':'Maintains the generated-job pen state and emits M3/M5 plus direction-specific dwell only when the requested state differs. It models commanded state; physical switch confirmation belongs to SetPen, not this G-code construction helper.',
'reproduce.py:WriteGcode':'Maps, decimates, orders and clamps paths, optionally closes near-rings and draws short endpoint bridges. It explicitly restates modal feed on travel and drawing transitions, counts lengths and writes an inspectable file. Its timing summary uses toggle count times the mean of up/down dwells and excludes some initial/final travel and execution overhead; it is nominal accounting, not a rigorous measured lower bound.',
'reproduce.py:Connect':'Claims the configured chip lines with gpiod v2, sets initial direction/step/motor states, and records the live handle. Failure must be interpreted as no connected controller; reading this function does not verify actual header wiring or GPIO current capability.',
'reproduce.py:RequestAbort':'Sets an event consumed inside motion/dwell loops. Requesting interruption and observing that the active job has stopped are separate events.',
'reproduce.py:EmergencyStop':'Requests abort, waits a bounded interval for the active-job event, turns outputs inactive and attempts pen-up/parking according to state. It returns whether execution remains active or latched. It does not supply a hard real-time maximum stop latency or guarantee the pen successfully raised.',
'reproduce.py:BresenhamMove':'The current default delay is MIN_STEP_DELAY_S, not the old circle-demo constant. It updates commanded counters after sequential GPIO pulses, checks abort/endstops per major iteration and distributes minor pulses through an integer error. A diagonal iteration can incur two pulse sleeps; the geometry algorithm alone does not enforce constant physical feed.',
'reproduce.py:SetPen':'First respects endstop interlocks unless forced, returns immediately if already at the requested feedback state, then runs the one-way motor until target/timeout and adds up-overrun only after successful pen-up. Returns success/failure. It cannot measure force, and the current G-code runner logs pen-confirmation failure but continues.',
'reproduce.py:_GcodeLinearMove':'Clamps the requested machine target, uses calibrated X/Y steps/mm and a switch-clearance offset, rounds to integer target steps, and computes nominal major-iteration delay from Euclidean length and F/60. It then calls sequential-pulse Bresenham. This explains direction-dependent timing overhead and why the feed is not a verified speed.',
'reproduce.py:_GcodeArcMove':'Converts an I/J-centred G2/G3 arc to short straight chords and executes them through the linear mover. Approximation depends on chord segmentation, and the current parser supports only its implemented dialect rather than every CNC command.',
'reproduce.py:RunGcodeFile':'Requires calibration, opens the job, initialises modal state and encloses execution in a finally block clearing _jobActive. Initial parser coordinates use nominal STEPS_PER_MM, whereas _GcodeLinearMove obtains physical coordinates from calibrated factors. Do not assume these are identical in every modal/no-coordinate case.',
'reproduce.py:_RunGcodeLines':'Processes commands with abort and endstop checks, modal feed and absolute/relative positioning. M3/M5 call SetPen; a false return is printed and execution continues. Unsupported commands are logged/skipped. Commanded parser targets and clamped/actually reached coordinates need not agree after interruptions; successful parsing is not independent position feedback.',
'train.py:InitLinear':'Uses uniform weights and biases between plus/minus one over the square root of input width, not the Gaussian initialiser described in the old function note. The distribution matches a common framework linear-layer convention; it is a starting distribution, not learned evidence.',
'train.py:InitLstmDirection':'Uses independent uniform gate matrices and both bias arrays between plus/minus one over square root of hidden size. The gate block layout must match inference. It does not explicitly set a positive forget-gate bias.',
'train.py:DecodeCrop':'Dispatches cached crop decoding using current byte representation and returns pixels for the ordinary preparation path. Cached and fresh files must not be conflated; cache format is an implementation contract.',
'web/server.py:ApiGenerate':'This endpoint expresses the intended full synthesis-to-job flow but has static interface conflicts in the captured tree: GantryConfig has no ignoreRuling field and RenderTrajectory accepts neither profile nor uniformInk. Explain the intended stages without claiming this snapshot successfully completes generation. No fix is made for this manual.',
'web/server.py:WordAcc':'Computes case-insensitive word-level longest-common-subsequence recall divided by reference word count. It is not standard word error rate and is not strict positional exact-word accuracy. The function now resides in the server rather than recognise.py.',
'web/server.py:ReadAllLines':'Reads up to three sampled crops upright and inverted using mean best-frame log score. It reuses the chosen probe reads and maps remaining jobs over LW.Map. If inversion wins it reverses line order and rotates each crop to keep text and metadata consistent.',
'web/server.py:NameWriter':'Maps independent crops through the configured namer, then averages full class-probability vectors weighted by counts of pixels below 128. The current LW configuration inherits the same model and stroke-normalisation flag. A page probability is a weighted arithmetic pool, not a product of independent likelihoods.',
'web/server.py:ApiClassify':'Applies upload/capture orientation handling, times SegmentLines as one combined stage, resolves inversion, reads and names lines, and emits paired metrics only where supplied truth is compatible. It does not report the earlier three separate conditioning/segmenting/cropping timings from the core API.',
'retrace.py:PageStrokes':'Calls SegmentLines(gray, timer=timer), although the captured core does not accept timer. If that mismatch were resolved elsewhere, the remaining path would still binarise, thin, trace and prune source ink; the code comment claiming only mechanical differences is stronger than this processing supports.',
'web/lineworkers.py:CanPool':'Allows a pool only when LINE_WORKERS is not one, at least MIN_LINES_FOR_POOL jobs are present, os.fork exists and configuration is nonempty. Eligibility uses the number of jobs passed to Map: after orientation probes this can be smaller than page line count.',
'web/lineworkers.py:_CapThreads':'Sets thread-count environment variables and tries seven OpenBLAS entry-point spellings (including SciPy-prefixed wheel symbols) found in NumPy shared libraries. It is a best-effort cap, not a portable guarantee for every BLAS/backend. Environment settings after initialisation alone may not reconfigure an already-loaded backend.',
'web/lineworkers.py:Map':'Uses an explicit fork multiprocessing context, creates a pool for the current map and returns results in supplied job order. Failures fall back to serial calls of the same function. Successful model inheritance does not remove crop/result IPC or pool-startup cost, and failure during a serial retry can still propagate.',
}

